{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "11", "x": 0.9125176099423778, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.02122563866125786, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING", "x": 0.42600617733351664, "y": 0.1588305063161454, "w": 0.13046256798557843, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 1", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.20881655694519488, "w": 0.2852801181661608, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1 - 13, which are based on Reading", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.24357687672603662, "w": 0.8261407720928716, "h": 0.01742835839970161, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Passage 1 below.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2698307395852367, "w": 0.15808640454521827, "h": 0.01742835839970161, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "The kākāpō", "x": 0.43507694446520573, "y": 0.32200455553713075, "w": 0.1727608524457789, "h": 0.026142547029900542, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "The kākāpō is a nocturnal, flightless parrot that is critically endangered and one", "x": 0.11251763813674019, "y": 0.36025793284656643, "w": 0.8158465362405719, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "of New Zealand's unique treasures", "x": 0.34154740195102934, "y": 0.3885883583634891, "w": 0.3582767062382231, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "The kākāpō, also known as the owl parrot, is a large, forest-dwelling bird, with a", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.44524905851176433, "w": 0.826595470262996, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "pale owl-like face. Up to 64 cm in length, it has predominantly yellow-green", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4736041538193891, "w": 0.8267650465365891, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "feathers, forward-facing eyes, a large grey beak, large blue feet, and relatively", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5019345416149192, "w": 0.8268694169395625, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "short wings and tail. It is the world's only flightless parrot, and is also possibly one", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5302649294104493, "w": 0.8262950721483479, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "of the world's longest-living birds, with a reported lifespan of up to 100 years.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.558595279484587, "w": 0.7891306991186853, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Kākāpō are solitary birds and tend to occupy the same home range for many years.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5867773090433719, "w": 0.826259803564239, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "They forage on the ground and climb high into trees. They often leap from trees", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6151076968389021, "w": 0.825741847497617, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "and flap their wings, but at best manage a controlled descent to the ground. They", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6434380846344322, "w": 0.8262512939930732, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "are entirely vegetarian, with their diet including the leaves, roots and bark of trees", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6718054771160155, "w": 0.8263382351538997, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "as well as bulbs, and fern fronds.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7001359026329381, "w": 0.33873427100605585, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Kakap6 breed in summer and autumn, but only in years when food is plentiful.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7284662527070758, "w": 0.8259031192499521, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Males play no part in incubation or chick-rearing - females alone incubate eggs", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7567966027812134, "w": 0.8264978665069738, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "and feed the chicks. The 1-4 eggs are laid in soil, which is repeatedly turned over", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.785127028298136, "w": 0.82676668693585, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "before and during incubation. The female kākāpō has to spend long periods away", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8134573783722736, "w": 0.8266131045550504, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "from the nest searching for food, which leaves the unattended eggs and chicks", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8417877284464113, "w": 0.825924649490251, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "particularly vulnerable to predators.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.870142823754036, "w": 0.3719937248576774, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}